{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795071936,"nonce":"3KowhpBkvTmm9frRb1/gIPrhsiA=","message":"ROOT CAUSE (peer DB data + code, 2026-11-19).\n\nWhat the data shows: every step got a tail lease, but steps whose Pod waited for a new Karpenter node had their lease expire 45s after the claim, never renewed, with 0 log_chunks. Steps on existing nodes have logs. The 0.4.1 run shows the same pattern.\n\nWhy:\n- For a Pod with no spec.nodeName, the API server answers a follow log request with 200 and an empty body (LogLocation returns an empty location; recalled from upstream, not re-verified).\n- PodLogChunks reads EOF, and log_tail.rs:306 treats Ok(()) as fully drained, so the fence is never retried and nothing is logged.\n- 0.4.1's unschedulable grace (1166c30) made this common.\n\nFix plan:\n(1) k8s log_stream returns a not-ready error while the Pod is unscheduled.\n(2) A 0-byte clean end is not drained; back off and retry.\n(3) INFO lines on tail start and end, with bytes.\nSeparate known gap: a 1-line step that ends inside the 3s backoff.","files":null}]}